.TH DAM 1.SH NAMEdam \- show a disk's allocation map.SH SYNOPSIS\fBdam\fR[device].SH DESCRIPTION\fBdam\fRdraws the allocation map of an RBF disk, the current one unless a deviceis named: one character a cluster, sixty-four to a line, each lineheaded by the number of its first cluster.  A\fB/\fRis a cluster that is allocated or defective, a blank one that is free,so fragmentation and free space can be seen at a glance..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOfree, howfrag, ssl